= 3. How the Test Case Works

*3.1 Physical layer (data generation).* Each meter is an independent device
model. Prosumers carry a 5–15 kW photovoltaic array modelled with clear-sky
irradiance, plane-of-array transposition, cell-temperature derate, and an
inverter model @pvlib; every meter carries a ZIP load with constant-impedance,
constant-current, and constant-power components responding to bus voltage. An
80-bus distribution topology is solved each fifteen-minute tick by
backward/forward-sweep alternating-current power flow @pandapower, yielding bus
voltages, line losses, transformer loading, and system frequency. Generation is
deterministic (fixed seed) and exported to a replay dataset; each case simulates
7 days × 96 ticks = 672 ticks per meter. Timestamps are historical, so the week
replays back-to-back with no inter-epoch waiting.

The resulting energy profile (@tbl-energy) grounds the physical realism of the
test. Per-prosumer generation is $approx 48$ kWh per day ($approx 333$–$347$ kWh
over the week), consistent with a 5–15 kW rooftop array under the seeded weather,
and near-identical across fleets because the profiles are seed-fixed. Per-meter
consumption is $approx 55$–$59$ kWh per day. Crucially the community is
*net-importing*: total consumption exceeds generation roughly seven- to
eight-fold, because only 15% of meters are prosumers — a consumer-heavy
residential feeder with rooftop solar, not a surplus microgrid. The raw
tick-surplus, $S_"raw" = sum_p sum_t max(0, g_(p,t) - c_(p,t))$ summed over
prosumers $p$ and ticks $t$, is the exportable energy before any cap. Two on-chain
filters then route it. First, the anomaly gate rejects implausible readings, so
only the gate-passing fraction is tokenisable. Second, the 10 kWh/day sell cap
binds on roughly three-quarters of prosumer-days (66 of 84, 122 of 168, 298 of
399, and 597 of 798 at 80, 160, 380, and 760 meters): the within-cap portion becomes tradeable
GRID and the cap-withheld remainder is certified as RECs, so
$E_"settle" + E_"REC"$ equals the gate-passing surplus and is bounded above by
metered generation (@eq-conserve). At 160 m, for instance, 5,107 kWh of raw
surplus yields 1,321 kWh traded plus 2,610 kWh certified — the balance being
readings the gate rejected. Every quantity scales near-linearly with fleet size,
confirming that the seed-fixed profiles isolate scale as the sole variable.

