Concretely, a dataset is three files. `meters.json` fixes each device's
identity; `readings.jsonl` holds one record per meter-tick — energy in
watt-hours per fifteen-minute interval, integer, exactly what the oracle
ingests; `daily.json` is the per-meter daily rollup (kilowatt-hours) that
drives order sizing. @fig-dataset shows the 80-meter export used in §4.7:
meter 2's photovoltaic output is zero before dawn, exceeds load mid-morning
(the exportable tick-surplus), and is *curtailed to exactly match load* once
the day's 5 kWh export cap is reached — visible as $g = c$ — so the daily
rollup's surplus field pins at the cap.

