*3.2 On-chain lifecycle.* (1) *Telemetry* — meter readings are submitted to the
oracle program in batches of up to ten instructions per transaction across
parallel per-meter chains; readings that trip the on-chain anomaly gate
(produced·100 > 1000·consumed) are sent individually so the rejection is
recorded on-ledger. (2) *Trading* — daily continuous-double-auction sessions
across 16 zone shards: each prosumer offers $min$(daily surplus, 10 kWh cap),
each consumer bids its actual consumption. (3) *Lifecycle* — per prosumer per
day: registry synchronisation and $"settle\_and\_mint"$ (GRID, an SPL
Token-2022 mint), escrow deposit, $"settle\_offchain\_match"$ with two inline
Ed25519 signature-verify instructions (versioned transaction with an
address-lookup table), buyer withdrawal, and burn. At week-end, cap-withheld
surplus is certified as renewable-energy certificates (RECs) via $"issue\_erc"$,
which enforces $"GRID" + "REC" <= "metered generation"$ on chain at a rate of
one REC token per megawatt-hour. Each case runs on a *freshly reset* validator
(programs redeployed, state re-bootstrapped) so fixed-identifier settlement
pollution cannot cross runs. @fig-dataflow traces one quantum of energy from the
physical model through every program it touches to final retirement.

