*4.2 Energy conservation closes exactly.* @tbl-cons shows the token accounting.
On uncontended runs the identity $E_"mint" = E_"settle" = E_"burn"$ (@eq-conserve)
holds to the atomic watt-hour: every minted GRID token settles against a real
Ed25519-signed counterparty match and is burned on delivery, with the
cap-withheld remainder certified as RECs. Settlement compute cost is
approximately 106 thousand CU per match — an order of magnitude above the
approximately 11 thousand CU of an order — reflecting the two inline signature
verifications.

